ed  to a lot of different  stories  that i might otherwise miss out on  because you know i have friends who will  say i like this this blog or i'm going  to link this msnbc article  or i'm going to tweet this this uh  article that i think is important  and  now there's not enough time to actually  read everything of course so i'm i'm  pretty selective in that and i suspect  that one of the things actually  i said i was going to close with talking  about social media what i'm going to  close with is this  one of the things that the  the techno sphere  makes us conscious of when it comes to  news  is just how little news we're actually  able to take yet  because if you're doing the sort of  strategies that i was talking about you  know having a variety of different news  sources and trying to go to them you're  not going to read every story you're not  going to follow up every possibility  you only have the same 24 hours a day  that you know back in 1940 people had  and back in 240 a.d people had and that  in  you know whatever time we pick in the  future people are going to have that's a  constant you only got so much time  so the question is which stories are you  going to  to allow to inform you by you doing the  work of you know clicking on them and  running your eyeballs over them and  trying to keep your your brain active  and parsing them  is that a bad thing  this this awareness  it could induce a kind of depression i  can't really know anything  you know i can't possibly follow things  it could induce a kind of anxiety i'm  always uh you know  i'm always out of the know when it comes  to important news items  i think it'd be better if it just  induces a kind of humility there's a lot  of things that we just don't know about  if we want to know  a lot more about this one that means  that all this other stuff has got to  wait or or not happen  and the news cycle constantly  keeps going on  i think that the more that you  that you consume news in a  self-conscio